STATUS -- what runs, and what it needs==============================================================Every program below was RUN, not merely built.   426  program files in /dd/CMDS and /dd/CMDS/GAMES, all of which RUN        (424 distinct names: gnuchess and wish exist in both directories,        as different builds)   339  of those files need nothing but this disk    87  of those files also need Microware's cio (and sometimes csl, math)        -- 86 distinct names, gnuchess being the one in both places     3  in /dd/CMDS/BROKEN -- do not run even with all three loaded    16  alternates in /dd/CMDS/REBUILT, 5 of them needing cioPrograms needing the Microware libraries are marked with a STAR before thename in DOC/INDEX.  (An older [libs] marker was removed: it was neverexplained anywhere, and it was wrong in both directions -- it blamed eightprograms that only wanted TERM set, and missed nine that do need cio.  Thestar list was measured by running every program on this disk with no ciopresent.)They are NOT kept in a separate directory: if you run OS-9 you already havecio, and sorting a collection by which libraries its authors linked againsthelps nobody browse it.  The star tells you which ones will ask for it.If you do not have them, everything unstarred still runs -- that is whatthis disk was originally built to guarantee, and it still holds.--------------------------------------------------------------NEEDS NOTHING -- 339 programs--------------------------------------------------------------  Built with cc -qm from the source in /dd/SRC, or already cio-free.  This is the set that runs with this disk as the only disk.--------------------------------------------------------------NEEDS cio / csl / math -- 86 names (87 files)--------------------------------------------------------------  NOT broken.  Compiled the ordinary way for the era (cc -qixm), which makes  the linker use the cio trap handler instead of linking stdio in.  I